      "result": "\n\nWrote the complete application to `submission/main.c`. It covers all requirements:\n\n- **Devices**: `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_ALIAS(led0))` and `DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_ALIAS(sw0))`, with a `device_is_ready` check.\n- **LED**: configured output, initially off via `GPIO_PIN_OUT_INIT_VAL`-less default — `GPIO_PIN_OUTPUT_INACTIVE` drives the pin off.\n- **Button**: `GPIO_INPUT | GPIO_PULL_UP`.\n- **Interrupt**: `gpio_init_callback` with `BIT(DT_GPIO_PIN(DT_ALIAS(sw0)))` mask, `gpio_add_callback_dt`, and `gpio_pin_interrupt_configure_dt(..., GPIO_INT_EDGE_BOTH)`.\n- **Callback**: toggles the LED with `gpio_pin_toggle_dt`.\n- **Main loop**: `k_sleep(K_FOREVER)` after setup.\n\nHeaders included: `zephyr/kernel.h` and `zephyr/drivers/gpio.h`. Note this uses the Zephyr 3.x per-pin API (device + pin), which matches the requested `*_dt` function set.",
